===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|blennius}}, {{m|la|blendius}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|βλεννός||mucus, slime}} (Modern Greek [[βλέννα]]), because of its slimy coating. From {{der|en|ine-pro|*mel-|t=soft}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛni|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|blennies}}

# A {{vern|true blenny}}, any of various marine fishes from the suborder [[Blennioidei]] that are generally small and elongated which dwell on the sea floor, including scaled and scaleless forms and dramatically divergent appearance, in several families.
